.TH tee "" "Command"
.SH NAME
tee \- branch pipe output
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtee [\-a] [\-i] [\fIfile\fB ...]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
tee -- branch pipe output
Usage:	tee  [ -a ] [ -i ]  [ file ... ]
Options:
	-a	Append to each output 'file'
	-i	Ignore interrupts
.HE
.B tee
copies its standard input to its standard output, and also copies it
to each
.I file
named.
It is meant to sit in the middle of a pipeline and split off a copy
of the data flowing through it.
.IP \fB\-a\fR
Append to each
.I file
instead of creating (truncating) it.
.IP \fB\-i\fR
Ignore interrupts, so that
.B tee
survives an interrupt that kills the rest of the pipeline.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B tee
complains and exits if it cannot create (or, with
.BR \-a ,
open for append) one of the named files, or if more than twenty
output files are given.
.SH NOTES
Unless
.B \-i
is given,
.B tee
exits on the first interrupt signal it receives.
